<title>DOMINICAN REPUBLIC: Three wounded during Dominican transport strike.</title>
<headline>Three wounded during Dominican transport strike.</headline>
<dateline>SANTO DOMINGO, Dominican Republic 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least two people were shot and wounded, many others arrested and two vehicles set on fire in Santo Domingo on Monday during a transportation workers' strike, police said.</p>
<p>The National Federation of Unified Transportation workers called for a boycott of passenger transportation to protest a delay in a special government subsidy paid to drivers.</p>
<p>Thousands of people were stranded by the driver's strike, mostly in the edges of the city. One of the two vehicles set on fire was a public bus.</p>
</text>
